    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Problem\r\nJava/Kotlin/Android developers navigating deeply nested, single-child directory structures face a \"navigation tax,\" having to repeatedly press `l` or `h` through empty intermediate directories.\r\n\r\n### Proposed Solution\r\nThis PR adds visual directory collapsing to `mini.files` when `content.collapse_single_child = true` is set (disabled by default).\r\n\r\n- **Forward Collapse**: Merges single-child directories visually (e.g. `a/b/c/`). Path index is registered to the leaf, allowing preview and selection (`l`) to jump straight to the nested files.\r\n- **Symmetric Navigation**: Pressing `h` climbs up all single-child folders in one step. Updated cursor decoding so `h` lands exactly on the collapsed line instead of reverting to line 1.\r\n- **Orphan Directory Cleanup**: Deletes/renames of collapsed leaves automatically clean up empty parent directories up to the buffer root path on synchronization, checking that parent buffers are not actively preserving them.\r\n- **Flicker Fix**: Replaced `children_path_ids` caching with `cached_children` to preserve custom collapsed names across window updates.\r\n\r\n### Verification\r\n- All existing tests pass.\r\n- Added 3 new unit test cases covering collapse rendering, reverse navigation, and directory cleanup.\r\n\r\n### Screenshots\r\n\r\nWhen config is false:\r\n<img width=\"1494\" height=\"271\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9e8fd1a8-9ee5-4c19-9f19-a5ded3cc88ff\" />\r\n\r\nWhen config is true:\r\n<img width=\"812\" height=\"248\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7dd35f6a-f198-466d-b4b8-8fa1e1340953\" />",
